A broken Angular build or red spec suite (Ionic/Capacitor included - `ionic build` wraps `ng build`) -
default to delegating rather than looping in-session: fix-the-build goes to
**`ng-build-error-resolver`**, make-the-tests-pass goes to **`angular-test-resolver`** once the build
is green. The dispatched seat absorbs the repeated build/test output and returns only a diagnosis,
which is the whole point: the red loop's noise stays out of this context.

A resolver that stops as BLOCKED_CONTRACT_CHANGE hit a fix needing a shared-contract change -
outside its bounded scope by design; route it through `project-solve-cross-task`, never edit the contract
to go green.

A seat with no dispatch tool (an implementer or a resolver) does NOT delegate - this routing policy
is the orchestrator's, owned by `project-solve-cross-task`; run your own bounded fix loop and report the red
per your cap. A diagnoser can dispatch, but its one sanctioned dispatch is the evidence-gatherer: it
names the resolver in its report, never dispatches one.

This is guidance, auto-attached by glob (not a hard block).
